\section{Discussion}
\paragraph{Look at the line, not the industry.} Errors concentrate in numbers whose unit sits in a header, on crowded lines, in later columns and in year-to-date periods, in every sector.
\paragraph{Give the model the unit.} The most dangerous case is a number whose unit is not on the page at all: the model guesses, and a digit-based check passes the guess. A reader system should carry the document's scale statement with every page, or verify the scale separately.
\paragraph{Think, don't retry.} Thinking reduces confident-wrong answers; retrying after a failed check increases them. The thinking budget must be large enough not to cut answers off.
\paragraph{Make the evidence check layout-tolerant.} A strict character-for-character check punishes formatting, not reading. Comparing the words and figures of a quote keeps the guarantee and removes the artefact.

\section{Limitations}
The tag effects are observational: we did not move a unit from a row label to a header and re-ask, although the regression holds the other tags fixed and R1 is a true intervention on layout. One hardware and serving configuration (RTX~4090 at 450\,W, vLLM~0.33, temperature~0). A fixed thinking budget cut off a fifth of Qwen3.5-9B's thinking answers. R1's rendering is imperfect: in << (100*d.r1_header_aligned)|num(0) >>\% of tables with a header, the last header row has as many cells as the first data row. The oil-and-gas analysis, the pipe-insensitive R1 grading and the cost-and-trust extension are exploratory. US filings only.

\section{Reproducibility and deviations}
The protocol, its seven logged deviations, the code, the frozen questions (fingerprint \texttt{9a007d80}), the Markdown pages of R1 (\texttt{7cdf066e}) and every model reply are public: code at \url{<< GITHUB >>}, data at \url{<< HF >>}. In a fresh clone, re-grading every stored reply reproduces every run summary byte for byte. The pre-registration commits are public in the Filing-Evidence repository. Deviations: (1)~a sampling rule changed to reach 10{,}000 questions, before any run; (2)~the cost-and-trust extension, exploratory; (3)~analysis code written after the runs, implementing the registered plan; (4)~the study moved to its own repository; (5)~details of R1--R3 and the 4-bit runs fixed before those runs; (6)~the pipe-insensitive R1 grading, exploratory; (7)~energy from the GPU counter rather than dedicated runs.

\section{Conclusion}
Across ten sectors and << d.answers_total|thou >> answers, the industry a number comes from matters little; how it is printed matters a great deal. Units away from the figure, crowded lines, later columns and year-to-date periods predict errors, and a number with no unit on the page invites a confident wrong guess that a quote check cannot see. Thinking helps, retrying does not, and evidence checks must tolerate layout.

